  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The paper focuses on the effect of cooling rates on pristine AgSbTe2. No extrinsic dopants were added to the samples. Thermoelectric properties were presented in plots (Fig 7 and Fig 8), but explicit numerical values for electrical conductivity, Seebeck coefficient, thermal conductivity, and power factor were not provided in the text or tables, except for the peak ZT value. [figure-pass p1-5] The paper focuses on pristine AgSbTe2 samples processed with different cooling rates (slow cooling, fast cooling, and quenching). No dopants were added to these samples. Thermoelectric properties were extracted from Fig. 7. [figure-pass p6-7] The provided figures show cyclical measurements of AgSbTe2 at constant temperatures (473 K and 623 K) to demonstrate stability. No doping was mentioned for these specific samples in the provided text. ",
